                <pb facs="0260" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg204"/>

                <head>No. 100.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to General Schenck</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-02-12"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 12,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>E. D. Winslow, charged with large forgeries, escaped by steamer Rotterdam, under
                    name of Clifton, and is said to be in London. Obtain arrest, if possible, and
                    advise Department promptly.</p>
                <closer><signed>FISH,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
